# Frozen evaluation datasets (architecture R.3, D16) are checked out with LF on
# every platform, so a Windows working tree (core.autocrlf=true) holds the same
# bytes as the Git blob and a Linux CI checkout. The integrity check itself does
# not depend on this: it hashes canonical content (UTF-8, CRLF as LF;
# src/reqpilot/domain/integrity.py). This file only removes the host-dependent
# working-tree representation for these files. Deliberately limited to data/gold;
# the rest of the repository keeps its existing convention.
data/gold/**/*.md    text eol=lf
data/gold/**/*.jsonl text eol=lf
data/gold/**/*.json  text eol=lf
data/gold/**/*.txt   text eol=lf
data/gold/**/*.yaml  text eol=lf
